  <!-- 05 — INTERVIEWS -->
  <div class="case-shell">
    <section class="case-section">
      <p class="sec-label">5. Interviews</p>

      <div class="hypotheses-intro">
        <h2 class="case-heading">
          Confirmed 3 hypotheses and identified a <em>key insight</em>
        </h2>
        <p class="case-body-text">
          Users struggled most with long sign-up and unclear onboarding, were
          concerned about unintended scheduled transfers, and preferred access to
          recent transactions over recent recipients.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="hypotheses-grid">
        <div class="hyp-card hyp-card--yes">
          <div class="hyp-status">Confirmed</div>
          <h4 class="hyp-title">Split registration and bank account opening</h4>
          <p class="hyp-note">Users wanted to explore before giving full KYC data.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hyp-card hyp-card--yes">
          <div class="hyp-status">Confirmed</div>
          <h4 class="hyp-title">Home screen as progressive onboarding</h4>
          <p class="hyp-note">Users needed clearer guidance after registration.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hyp-card hyp-card--yes">
          <div class="hyp-status">
            <span>Confirmed</span>
            <span class="hyp-badge">Insight</span>
          </div>
          <h4 class="hyp-title">Scheduled transfers with <span style="background:rgba(255,255,255,0.15);padding:0.05rem 0.45rem;border-radius:100px;white-space:nowrap;">confirmation control</span></h4>
          <p class="hyp-note">Users wanted automation without silent money movement.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hyp-card hyp-card--no">
          <div class="hyp-status">Not confirmed</div>
          <h4 class="hyp-title">Quick transfers to recent recipients</h4>
          <p class="hyp-note">Users showed more interest in recent transactions.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- AI in the loop -->
      <div class="ai-loop">
        <div class="ai-loop-header">AI in the loop</div>
        <div class="ai-loop-steps">
          <div>
            <p class="ai-step-num">1. Hypothesis refinement</p>
            <p class="ai-step-body">Helped sharpen each opportunity into a specific assumption to validate in interviews.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="ai-step-num">2. Question check</p>
            <p class="ai-step-body">Checked questions for bias and assumptions using The Mom Test principles.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="ai-step-num">3. Transcript structuring</p>
            <p class="ai-step-body">Transcribed Zoom calls and grouped answers by question.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="ai-step-num">4. Evidence tagging</p>
            <p class="ai-step-body">Tagged responses as strong, weak or no support for each hypothesis.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <!-- 06 — KEY UX DECISIONS -->
  <div class="case-shell" id="decisions">
    <section class="case-section">
      <p class="sec-label">6. Key UX decisions</p>
      <h2 class="case-heading">Three decisions that shape the product.</h2>

      <!-- Decision 01 -->
      <div class="decision-article">
        <div>
          <h3 class="decision-title">1. Split registration from bank account opening.</h3>
          <p class="decision-body">
            The user can sign up, browse and use lightweight features without
            committing to a full KYC flow up front. Account opening becomes contextual.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="compare-pair">
          <div class="compare-card compare-card--before">
            <p class="compare-label">Before</p>
            <ol style="list-style:none;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0.6rem;font-size:1.1rem;line-height:1.25;color:var(--muted);">
              <li>1. Sign up</li>
              <li>2. ID verification</li>
              <li>3. Address proof</li>
              <li>4. Account opening</li>
              <li style="text-decoration:line-through;opacity:0.5;">5. First useful action</li>
            </ol>
            <span class="compare-badge">~10 min to value</span>
          </div>
          <div class="compare-card compare-card--after">
            <p class="compare-label">After</p>
            <ol style="list-style:none;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0.6rem;font-size:1.1rem;line-height:1.25;">
              <li>1. Short registration</li>
              <li>2. Guided home screen</li>
              <li>3. First useful action</li>
              <li>4. Account opening later</li>
            </ol>
            <span class="compare-badge">~3 min to value</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Decision 02 -->
      <div class="decision-article">
        <div>
          <h3 class="decision-title">2. Home screen as progressive onboarding.</h3>
          <p class="decision-body">
            The home screen is a dashboard and a discovery layer at the same time.
            It surfaces the next meaningful action based on what the user has already done.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="decision-img-pair">
          <img src="/assets/img/initial-home.png"
               alt="UNIC Bank initial home screen with zero balance and prominent Open bank account call to action." />
          <img src="/assets/img/home-screen-4.png"
               alt="UNIC Bank home screen after account opening showing balance, IBAN and recent transactions." />
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Decision 03 -->
      <div class="decision-article">
        <div>
          <h3 class="decision-title">3. Scheduled transfers with confirmation.</h3>
          <p class="decision-body">
            Users can choose to receive a confirmation notification before each scheduled
            transfer is executed. Automation stays convenient, while users remain in control.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="decision-img-triple">
          <img src="/assets/img/scheduled-create.png"
               alt="UNIC Bank create scheduled transfer screen showing payment details, monthly frequency and required confirmation." />
          <img src="/assets/img/scheduled-notification.png"
               alt="iOS lock screen push notification prompting the user to confirm a scheduled transfer to Leo Smith." />
          <img src="/assets/img/scheduled-review.png"
               alt="UNIC Bank review transfer details screen with a Confirm transfer button at the bottom." />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

